The shopkeeper finishes my form.
He gives me the new SIM card.
The shopkeeper says, "Madam, this is your new number."
I say, "Thank you, bhaiya."
Now I have an Indian phone number.
I am very happy.
I put the SIM card in my phone.
The phone turns on.
Now I have network on my phone.
I look at my number on the packet.
I memorize my new number.
I read the number aloud.
"Nine eight seven six five."
"Four three two one zero."
This number is very easy.
I say it one more time.
"Nine eight seven six five, four three two one zero."
Now I remember my new number.
